    {
      "text": "You can test an orchestration rule to validate if the rule conditions match a set of events. You can use a set of events from the exported event logs JSON file, or automatically add a sample event to test a rule."
    },
    {
      "text": "To test a rule:"
    },
    {
      "item": "Go to Orchestrate > Rules.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          6,
          17
        ],
        [
          20,
          25
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Locate a rule to test, and then click the Edit icon.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 2,
      "strong": [
        [
          42,
          46
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "See image.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "In the Rule Details window, under General, click the here link.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 3,
      "strong": [
        [
          7,
          19
        ],
        [
          34,
          41
        ],
        [
          53,
          57
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "See image.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "In the Test Rules window, in the Events field, copy and paste the events in the JSON format, or click Add sample event to automatically add an event.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 4,
      "strong": [
        [
          7,
          17
        ],
        [
          33,
          39
        ],
        [
          102,
          118
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "See image.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "The All events passed message appears if the rule conditions match with the events.",
      "depth": 0,
      "strong": [
        [
          4,
          21
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "See image.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "Click Cancel to close the window.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 5,
      "strong": [
        [
          6,
          12
        ]
      ]
    }
  ]
}
